      "properties": {
        "snippet": "Governor Henry McMaster has set an ambitious agenda to conserve a total of 10 million acres across the state of South Carolina by 2027.\n\nTo accomplish this ambitious goal, the state's land management, conservation and natural resources agencies, along with numerous partner organizations, have collaborated to create a prioritization tool which identifies areas important to the state for protection. The backbone of conservation priorities in the state is driven by the SC Conservation Bank's Priority Analysis, updated annually. Priority areas from partner agencies and organizations are combined and modelled to derive statewide priorities.",
